invariant: INV-29
file: handshake_flight.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the client files its key log lines under the ClientHello random
  read after the key exchange wiped it, so every line carries 32 zero
  bytes while the server's carry the real value. The secrets still match,
  so a check that compares only secrets passes; a capture tool then finds
  two logs for two different connections. This is the first key log
  build's own bug, and tcp_nonblocking_loop_test compares the random both ends log.

--- old
    memcpy(h->client_random, h->random, sizeof h->client_random);
--- new
    (void)h->random;
